Bragging almost done, here is what happened.

Camped quite a while at the altar in mine town, after converting it
accidentally (!). Had no single other altar until dl20, got used to that
one in mine town, though it was to Set, not Crom. Totally forgot about
that and once offered some monster, and was shocked about the whole
thing that happened, never even tried a conversion before. Went out
lucky anyway.

Being a packrat, i did a real lot of carrying things from there to base
camp at level 21, and accumulated quite a pile of scrolls, potions and
wands there. At that time i was quite certain to make it, if no mishaps
kicked in.

>From the castle (dl30) downward (dl 49) until the run with the amulet,
the whole story was pretty much boring, any bunch of monsters could
hardly do any severe physical damage to me any more and was merely
standing in my way, had more to worry about the Demogorgon team. Most of
the time i wielded my pick axe because i was too lazy switching to
frostbrand every time.

At astral i tried desperately to remember how to deal with death. He was
sitting next to me, draining maxHP. Zapped him two times with /oT, but
nothing happened. Was unsure if he wasn't teleportable at all or if
simply boths wands were empty at that time. Finally decided to pull out
a third one from my boH before having to melee him and gladly beamed him
some steps away. Middle altar was the right one, i started out left.

Left behind huges piles of things at base camp, >50K gold, for or so
granted artifacts and gems, this thing wasn't about score, but about
surviving (while not being burdened). Again carried an "oLS in the bag,
but never thought about using it on the planes, totally forgot about
that in the whole hassle there.

Inspired by 'Ellora The Elven Ranger' i decided writing down the story
real time. Now i even more appreciate the whole work done by Krysia back
in 2004, its a must read, and i know i did not manage anything
comparable to that story, neither in yield nor in substance. Guess i am
way too spoiled afer all the years of nethack. But still i tried my
best, delivering 24 chapters of the story, the last one being some
aftermath. As most of you might have guessed by now, i did not do it in
english, just because writing in german on the fly while gaming still is
way faster for me than doing the same thing in english.

I am currently publishing the chapters one by one on a blog at
twoday.net, starting with http://castagir.twoday.net/20090921. No
offense meant by posting the link, suppose i can't post here in anything
but english. The first 17 chapters are online now, the rest is about to
follow the next days, still have to fix tons of typos made in the hurry.
Would love to hear if someone capable of reading it likes it or not. It
really was an experience to stop gaming every now and then, writing down
what happened lately. Constantly had to stop myself from running too far
and having to cope up with too many things which happened in the meantime.

After the castle the plot pretty much shortens, not much special happens
down there except vlad, rodney and the invocation, and the description
of loads of maces sure is no fun reading ... nor writing.

